1
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:17,060
Summer has come again this year.

2
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:19,680
It's here, it's here,
it's here, it's here, it's here!

3
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,980
Summer has come again this year.

4
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:25,020
It's here, it's here, it's here, it's here!

5
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:28,580
Big ones, small ones,
the tide pools' little ripples,

6
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:34,420
Big ones, small ones,
the tide pools' little ripples,

7
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:35,800
Rising tide,

8
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,840
Summer has come again this year.

9
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:43,380
It's here, it's here,
it's here, it's here, it's here!

10
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:46,700
Summer has come again this year.

11
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,800
Hahaha, hahaha, hahaha,
hahaha, hahaha, hahaha!

12
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,220
Big waves, small waves,
tiny little waves, about that size,

13
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:55,080
good even in the southern wind.

14
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:58,400
Big bottoms, small bottoms,
tiny little ones, about that size,

15
00:00:58,400 --> 00:00:59,180
Full speed ahead!

16
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:13,600
In the southern wind, in the southern wind,

17
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:20,540
on the shore, dreamily slow,
on the shore, dreamily slow,

18
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:22,020
crumble, crumble, crumble,
crumble, crumble, crumble,

19
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:23,380
splash!

20
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:31,560
Wake up, hibernating cop!

21
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:39,900
The Olympic flame that kept burning over
Atlanta's skies is now quietly going out.

22
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:43,540
See you in four years,
at the next Games in Sydney.

23
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:46,480
The Olympic flame that kept burning over
Atlanta's skies is now quietly going out.

24
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,780
But somehow,
it feels like something's missing.

25
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:52,880
Something's missing? The number of medals?

26
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:53,860
Not that.

27
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:57,280
When it comes to the Olympics,
there's always something, right?

28
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:58,660
Olympic temperature?

29
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,220
The Minami Haru from the Tokyo Olympics was great,
wasn't it?

30
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:06,720
No, there was something with more impact,
like this.

31
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:09,960
The one where women pat
powder onto their faces.

32
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:11,920
That's the compact.

33
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:15,760
It's right on the tip of my tongue,
but I can't remember.

34
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:21,720
That's right, it's a cicada!

35
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:23,680
It's something to do with cicadas.

36
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:26,760
Cicadas?
The one singing now is an Abura-zemi, right?

37
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:28,600
It's not an Abura-zemi.

38
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:31,420
Then is it a Tsukutsukuboshi?

39
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:34,020
It's getting closer.

40
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:35,920
Was there another one?

41
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,900
The one that goes "kanakana"!

42
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:41,460
A dumbass cicada that can't sing in kanji?

43
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:45,280
No, not that. It's a Higurashi.

44
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:50,380
Higurashi! Right, we forgot about him.

45
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:54,220
No wonder, it's like the Olympics,
once every four years.

46
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,860
Has it really been four years already?

47
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:58,320
What are you talking about?

48
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:00,751
At this police box,

49
00:03:00,801 --> 00:03:04,200
besides us, there's a guy
named Higurashi who works here.

50
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,480
What!?

51
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:07,600
I've never heard of that person.

52
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:08,480
Me neither.

53
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:11,535
You two started working here

54
00:03:11,585 --> 00:03:13,360
recently, so of course you wouldn't know.

55
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,420
I suppose not.

56
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:18,100
The last time he came to work was

57
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:21,660
the year of the Barcelona Olympics,
four years ago.

58
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:25,500
So he's been absent for four years straight?

59
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:28,400
Higurashi is a real lazy bones,
I'll tell you that.

60
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:30,760
He's been skipping work
since the day he joined.

61
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:33,780
He only came in about three days a month.

62
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:35,640
And then it gradually escalated.

63
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:38,920
Now he only shows up once every four years.

64
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,180
Once every four years.

65
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:44,440
Yeah, that's why he's also
called the Olympics man.

66
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:45,720
I can't believe it.

67
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:49,140
To think there's a bigger
lazybones than Ryo-chan!

68
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:51,180
How haven't you been fired?

69
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:54,420
Higurashi has a special ability.

70
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:55,780
A special ability?

71
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:58,060
You'll understand if you bring him here.

72
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,440
I-I'll pass.

73
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:05,300
You're the only one who knows Higurashi.

74
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,580
Hurry up and go get him.

75
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:10,320
Sorry to keep you waiting.

76
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:21,640
Senpai, we're only going to wake him up,

77
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:24,460
so why do we need all this heavy gear?

78
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:26,580
You'll see when we get there.

79
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:38,520
Did Higurashi live in the
same dorm as you, senpai?

80
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:50,760
I think it was this room.

81
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:57,657
Don't worry,

82
00:04:57,707 --> 00:05:00,520
It's a storeroom.

83
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,920
This isn't a storeroom!

84
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,860
Someone's actually living here.

85
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:09,820
This is it.

86
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:13,060
Sure enough, it's rusted shut.

87
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:17,960
Nakagawa, pry the door open!

88
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:18,400
Yes.

89
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:30,040
Move aside, Nakagawa.

90
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:38,120
Hey, Higurashi, are you in there?

91
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,800
This doesn't look like a
place where a human could live.

92
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:53,380
He's been left alone for four years doing nothing,
after all.

93
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:56,260
But it's so dark I can't see a thing.

94
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:57,980
Nakagawa, open the shutters.

95
00:05:58,820 --> 00:05:59,140
Yes.

96
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:06,660
Ow

97
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:09,660
Yaaah!

98
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:18,540
Whoa, something's stuck to my face! Hey, what are you doing?
Didn't you used to be scared of spiders and couldn't be a police officer?

99
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:20,960
Aaaaaah!

100
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:31,280
Bats swarming everywhere!

101
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:33,480
It's too bright!

102
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,100
Cherry blossoms, cherry blossoms!

103
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:38,120
What a troublesome guy.

104
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,620
Lend him Nakagawa.

105
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:42,480
Here you go.

106
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:44,040
That was a lifesaver.

107
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:47,540
This guy reacts like a
vampire every time you wake him.

108
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:49,400
Is that you, Ryotsu?

109
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:52,340
We came to pick you up.

110
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:55,120
What? It's still summer of Heisei 4?

111
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:57,860
No, I only dozed off a little,
so shouldn't it be autumn?

112
00:06:57,860 --> 00:07:01,380
Autumn passed long ago.
It's Heisei 8 this year.

113
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:02,060
No way.

114
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:06,240
Then what happened to the Japan New
Party that was founded and became a boom?

115
00:07:07,140 --> 00:07:09,080
That party died ages ago, you know.

116
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:10,160
What?

117
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:13,460
Then what about the LDP that was in turmoil?

118
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:17,320
Well, some of them broke away
and formed a different party.

119
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:21,140
So the prime minister isn't Miyazawa?

120
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:22,500
Miyazawa?

121
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:25,120
Right. It was like that four years ago.

122
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:27,475
While you were asleep, it was Hosokawa-san,

123
00:07:27,525 --> 00:07:29,760
then Hata-san, then Murayama-san.

124
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,260
Now it's Hashimoto-san.

125
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:32,820
It's changed that much?

126
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:34,680
The Tokyo governor is Yukio Aoshima,
you know.

127
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:36,800
Trying to trick me won't work.

128
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:40,660
I bet you're going to say the Osaka
governor is Knock Yokoyama, too.

129
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:43,480
Whoa, ding-ding! You got that fast.

130
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:45,060
Is that really true?

131
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:48,220
Then what happened to
Wakahanada and Takahanada?

132
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:51,160
Then they must have changed their
names to Wakanohana and Takanohana.

133
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:54,860
The older brother became an ozeki,
and the younger one became a yokozuna.

134
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:59,600
Has the world really changed that much?

135
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:02,800
You're like Urashima Taro.

136
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:06,540
Ryotsu, who's that young guy?

137
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:09,620
That's Nakagawa,
who joined the police box this year.

138
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:13,180
Anyway, stop sleeping and get up already.

139
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:17,340
Don't say that, it'll hit my empty stomach.

140
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:19,360
First, let's get something to eat.

141
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:28,120
No good, I've got no strength,
somebody push me up!

142
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:32,920
This fridge is broken.

143
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:36,520
Are the rice balls and bread
I bought before bed no good?

144
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:38,300
Yeah, they've all dried out.

145
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:39,560
What about the milk?

146
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Of course it's no good.

147
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,260
It's heavy.

148
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:42,800
What?

149
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:45,240
It's gone sour.

150
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:45,980
Lucky!

151
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:47,920
This is fine to eat.

152
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:49,000
How about you too?

153
00:08:49,740 --> 00:08:51,120
No thanks.

154
00:08:51,620 --> 00:08:53,280
You're so polite, aren't you.

155
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:56,300
Then watch TV or something
until we've finished eating.

156
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:05,220
You can watch it lying down, you know.

157
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,020
And next,

158
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:10,120
Spit it out quickly.

159
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:13,120
Ryotsu, sorry,
but could you take me to the private bath?

160
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:15,860
Where's a bath in this room?

161
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:21,080
The w-washing machine is the bath?

162
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:28,900
You, put the sheets and pillowcases in.
I'll wash them together.

163
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:29,780
Yeah.

164
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:33,660
Yes.

165
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:36,080
Yes.

166
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:39,660
While you're at it,
switch the water flow to reverse.

167
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:42,380
This reverse setting is the best.

168
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:44,220
It feels really good.

169
00:09:45,660 --> 00:09:47,340
The ultimate in laziness

170
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:54,100
Change into this.

171
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:55,900
Sorry, but

172
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:57,580
could you spread it out for me?

173
00:09:58,320 --> 00:10:00,480
This one's probably going to be a hassle.

174
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:01,780
Oof, there we go.

175
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,000
Are you all right?

176
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:13,120
Still, my body feels sluggish.
Maybe I just haven't had enough sleep.

177
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,600
You've been sleeping too much,
that's what it is.

178
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,560
Do you think so?

179
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:19,120
This way.

180
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:19,620
Sorry.

181
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:26,440
Are you okay?

182
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:31,160
When did they build stairs
in a place like this?

183
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:38,280
They've been here forever, we just forgot about them.
Come to think of it, I think I fell down them four years ago too.

184
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:43,960
You fell down eight years ago and twelve years ago too.
So it's your usual routine

185
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:52,660
What, didn't you come by patrol car?
It's a fifteen-minute walk. Let's go.

186
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:56,000
Let's just go in the car I bought.

187
00:10:56,540 --> 00:10:58,760
Since when do you have a car?

188
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:10,160
Isn't that a discontinued VW Beetle?
And it's brand new!

189
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:16,280
No, I bought it 20 years ago. I've only driven it twice,
so of course it's brand new.

190
00:11:18,020 --> 00:11:20,460
Downstairs? Wouldn't a taxi be better?

191
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:23,080
It's a hassle to flag one down.
Come on, get in.

192
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:32,960
It's scary that the odometer's
only at three kilometers.

193
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:36,000
It's never left the neighborhood, after all.

194
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,140
Alright, let's go.

195
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:40,420
Whoa, the engine started.

196
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:42,500
Now, how did it go again?

197
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:45,840
You press the clutch and put
the shift lever into first gear.

198
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,780
That's right, that's right.

199
00:11:48,020 --> 00:11:50,020
The clutch is...

200
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:03,880
To wreck a brand-new-looking
car in three seconds...

201
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,740
That's... that's incredible...

202
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:09,360
But I'm wide awake now...

203
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:19,080
I've brought the Chief.

204
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:20,060
Good work.

205
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:22,740
Walking like this after
so long has worn me out.

206
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:23,600
I'm going back to sleep.

207
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:26,100
You're as lazy as ever.

208
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:27,920
You haven't changed since four years ago.

209
00:12:28,460 --> 00:12:31,160
Honestly, you're such a troublesome guy.

210
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:34,520
Come on, wake up, Higurashi!

211
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:36,140
Yeah, yeah, I'm awake.

212
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:37,980
At least greet the Chief.

213
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:41,166
Chief, long time no see.

214
00:12:41,216 --> 00:12:43,580
You're still a senior patrol officer?

215
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:45,000
Mind your own business.

216
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:48,600
This is Terai,
who was transferred here three years ago.

217
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:50,440
Hi, I'm Higurashi.

218
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:51,800
Yeah, nice to meet you.

219
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:55,960
I'm a big fan of Risa Miyazawa.

220
00:12:56,260 --> 00:13:00,188
I recently bought that hugely popular photo book,
"Yonta Fe,"

221
00:13:00,238 --> 00:13:01,860
let's look at it together sometime.

222
00:13:02,540 --> 00:13:06,440
Right. Enough with the
photo book talk already.

223
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:08,060
Next...

224
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:08,400
I'm back.

225
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,780
Reiko, let me introduce you!

226
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:14,060
So this is the one you've
been hearing about...

227
00:13:14,060 --> 00:13:15,520
Eh eh, here you go!

228
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:22,080
Wake up, wake up, wake up!

229
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:23,420
Shakeen!

230
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:30,100
Hello, I'm Higurashi. People call
me Sonohigurashi. Nice to meet you!

231
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,800
Th-the pleasure is mine, I'm Reiko Akimoto.

232
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:35,400
Yes, Higurashi is fully awake!

233
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,880
Phew, he's weak around women.

234
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:45,360
I can feel it.

235
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:46,680
What is this energy?

236
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,400
A case is calling me.

237
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:50,660
What on earth happened to you?

238
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:53,260
Now Higurashi is finally
showing his true colors!

239
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:54,360
Impressive.

240
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:56,440
Bring me the unsolved case files.

241
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:57,200
Yes.

242
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:06,400
The first one is the missing man

243
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:16,320
I see him. This man is working at a construction site in Yamagata City,
in Tohoku.

244
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:19,720
Terai, contact the main station right away.

245
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:23,420
Yes, this is Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box 8.

246
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:25,300
Mr. Higurashi has woken up.

247
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:28,560
The second case is a jewel thief

248
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:33,280
The culprit is named Nakayama, and he's
hiding in a condo by the Sumida River.

249
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:40,520
Yamada of the serial Ōkā squad is
hiding in an apartment in Fukagawa.

250
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:45,200
Next, marriage fraudster Suzuki is
hiding at Kaminarimon in Asakusa.

251
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:46,600
That's amazing.

252
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:48,180
That's clairvoyance, isn't it?

253
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:53,000
Higurashi solves unsolved cases
like this every time he wakes up.

254
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:59,360
Next, next, next, next, next, next

255
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:04,180
I'm tired. I'm getting sleepy.

256
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:08,700
Damn it, you idiot, you haven't even
worked off four years' worth yet!

257
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:14,140
I'll give your shoulders a little massage.
Thanks for your hard work.

258
00:15:15,220 --> 00:15:19,100
Higurashi-san, you really do
have an amazing ability Alright.

259
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:22,880
Four cameras! Watch out!

260
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:29,320
I can see it, I can see it!

261
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:30,640
What are you doing?

262
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:31,980
It's nensha, thought photography.

263
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:35,160
Higurashi can capture incidents

264
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:36,860
that will happen within the next 24 hours.

265
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:39,240
You can even do that?

266
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:56,640
I wonder what's actually in this picture.

267
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:01,960
It's an underwear thief!

268
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:04,660
We've had a lot of incidents
inside the building lately.

269
00:16:05,260 --> 00:16:08,320
But from this photo,
we can't tell who the culprit is.

270
00:16:09,040 --> 00:16:12,300
Blurred into a shadow like that,
he must be incredibly quick.

271
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:15,580
So, with this photo this time...

272
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:17,500
Yaaah!

273
00:16:18,740 --> 00:16:20,180
Yaaah!

274
00:16:20,180 --> 00:16:22,000
Yaaah!

275
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:37,260
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!

276
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:44,040
It's just a dog! It's a dog that always barks at me on patrol.
Alright, go on, off you go.

277
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:59,440
Is this the house? Isn't this the one that's
filed the most reports of stolen underwear?

278
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:05,160
Living the high life The people in
this house are such awful Amuraa women.

279
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:07,560
Amuraa? What's that supposed to be?

280
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:12,960
Amuraa refers to the fashion fans of the top idol,
Amuro Nanae.

281
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:17,160
W-what?
Isn't the top idol Miyazawa Risa-chan?

282
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:20,280
Risa-chan got too thin,
so she's recharging right now.

283
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:21,580
N-no way.

284
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,440
Don't be so down, Higurashi.

285
00:17:23,940 --> 00:17:24,540
Let's go.

286
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:33,040
Why would our Taku-chan be the culprit?

287
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:37,480
You can't catch the real criminal, so
you're just pinning it on him, aren't you?

288
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:38,800
What?

289
00:17:49,180 --> 00:17:50,680
What the... what is this?

290
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:53,400
Higurashi also has the power of clay.

291
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:01,680
It's a hole.

292
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:07,300
It's the stolen underwear.

293
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,000
No way...

294
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:12,040
It was Igurasu-san, wasn't it?

295
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:14,440
I sense it again!

296
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:16,560
Nakagawa, the camera!

297
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:17,320
Yes!

298
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:21,600
Now it's a bank robbery?

299
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,680
I recognize this bank.

300
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:25,100
It's the bank in front of the station.

301
00:18:25,100 --> 00:18:27,260
Look, the clock is in the picture too.

302
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,340
Five minutes to three

303
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:31,880
We only have ten minutes left!

304
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:33,400
Alright, Reiko!

305
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:36,920
Terai's going straight to the bank,
so I'm leaving this to you!

306
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:37,960
Got it!

307
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:40,640
Hurry up, Nakagawa!

308
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:41,200
Yes!

309
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:05,300
Everyone, hands up!

310
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,800
Hand over the money quietly!

311
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:10,900
Welcome!

312
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:13,160
Gii! It's a gorilla!

313
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:14,580
What do you mean, gorilla!

314
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:15,740
You bastard!

315
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:17,480
Senpai!

316
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:25,040
Damn it, you're in the way!

317
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:26,580
You're going to die!

318
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:29,440
W-what?

319
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:30,600
Now!

320
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:31,580
There!

321
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:35,300
Handcuffs!

322
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:37,460
Hey, Higurashi! Put the cuffs on him!

323
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:40,620
Visor's sleeping!

324
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:45,380
Good job, everyone.

325
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:49,340
But Higurashi-san,
you really do have an amazing ability.

326
00:19:49,780 --> 00:19:51,700
Now I understand why you haven't been fired.

327
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:53,980
Where's Higurashi?

328
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:56,140
He was here until just now.

329
00:19:58,140 --> 00:20:00,020
I'm tired, I can't do this anymore.

330
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:03,340
If we can't do all the races,
just the main race is fine.

331
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:06,860
Use your nensha to tell me which
numbers finish first and second.

332
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:08,880
What are you doing?

333
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:13,320
Chief.

334
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:15,320
No, I was asking Higurashi for one more.

335
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:17,820
We were just trying to
have him solve a case.

336
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:20,460
Since when do cases have
first and second place?

337
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:21,880
So you were listening?

338
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:31,600
I sense it, I sense it!

339
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:33,580
Which horse numbers are they?

340
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:34,560
You idiot!

341
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:37,000
So it really is horse race predictions.

342
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:45,560
You...

343
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:52,660
That's me getting hit by a truck.

344
00:20:54,280 --> 00:20:56,120
That's definitely Ryotsu.

345
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:57,600
What an ominous photo.

346
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:00,480
Hey, Higurashi.

347
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:03,600
What grudge do you have against
me to take a photo like this?

348
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:06,880
It's not necessarily fatal, you know.

349
00:21:07,380 --> 00:21:09,140
Maybe the traffic jam will save me.

350
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:10,860
That's not reassuring at all.

351
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:13,120
Either way, it's still fascinating.

352
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:15,180
Ryotsu, don't worry about it.

353
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:16,840
Mistakes happen.

354
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:19,440
My ability is perfect,
and I'm confident in it, but

355
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:22,040
Maybe it's wrong about one
in several hundred million?

356
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:25,460
Are you encouraging me or bragging?

357
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:27,680
I absolutely don't believe it, you know.

358
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:30,180
Says the guy whose face is deathly pale!

359
00:21:30,740 --> 00:21:31,740
I'm not joking.

360
00:21:33,140 --> 00:21:35,760
Senpai, judging by the photo,
it's outside, so

361
00:21:35,810 --> 00:21:38,660
as long as you stay indoors for 24 hours,
you'll be safe.

362
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:42,240
Shut up! How can I work as a
cop if I'm scared of premonitions?

363
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,680
I absolutely don't believe it!

364
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:46,900
Senpai!

365
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:48,360
Ryo-chan, no!

366
00:21:48,660 --> 00:21:50,340
Shut up! Leave me alone!

367
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:52,820
I told you it's dangerous to go outside!

368
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:54,740
Throwing this stuff outside...

369
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:57,420
Senpai!

370
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:00,340
Ryo-chan!

371
00:22:01,740 --> 00:22:02,660
Are you all right, senpai?

372
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:05,200
Ow ow!

373
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,620
So, this photo is...

374
00:22:08,060 --> 00:22:12,620
the moment you walked
right into a stopped truck

375
00:22:14,360 --> 00:22:15,580
Hey, Higurashi!

376
00:22:15,760 --> 00:22:17,820
Go back to sleep for a million years or so!

377
00:22:17,940 --> 00:22:18,940
Don't you dare wake up again!

378
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:19,860
You idiot!

379
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:22,000
I'll do just that.

380
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,680
Chief, before that...

381
00:22:23,680 --> 00:22:25,360
The usual ritual

382
00:22:25,780 --> 00:22:26,460
Reiko-kun.

383
00:22:26,460 --> 00:22:27,850
Ten servings of tendon,

384
00:22:27,900 --> 00:22:30,780
ten servings of unadon,
and twenty servings of yakiniku.

385
00:22:32,740 --> 00:22:33,580
Go ahead and order them.

386
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:45,240
Heave-ho!

387
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:48,340
Everyone, carry him into the back room.

388
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:49,620
Hup!

389
00:22:57,220 --> 00:22:58,260
What an appetite.

390
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:01,300
He's going to sleep for four years,
so he's stocking up on food.

391
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:04,280
He's like a bear before hibernation.

392
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:10,640
Honestly.

393
00:23:18,260 --> 00:23:20,700
How can anyone get this fat?

394
00:23:21,250 --> 00:23:22,440
He looks like a different person.

395
00:23:23,940 --> 00:23:26,120
Well then, see you in four years.

396
00:23:26,770 --> 00:23:27,300
Shut up!

397
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:28,840
I'm going home to sleep.

398
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:30,600
Well, then.

399
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:33,160
See you tomorrow.

400
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:34,640
Good night.

401
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:37,660
Next time we meet, it'll be the year 2000.

402
00:23:37,660 --> 00:23:39,840
I can't wait for the next Olympics.

403
00:23:40,260 --> 00:23:41,120
Don't joke around.

404
00:23:41,120 --> 00:23:43,800
Try putting yourself in our shoes,
having to go wake him up.

405
00:23:44,120 --> 00:23:45,220
You've got a point there.

406
00:24:03,620 --> 00:24:05,920
Does everyone know about Katsutoki Bridge?

407
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:08,780
When a big ship comes through,
the bridge splits right down the middle

408
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:10,980
and rises up with a rumble.

409
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:13,600
Sadly, it doesn't open anymore.

410
00:24:13,600 --> 00:24:15,100
This Katsutoki Bridge

411
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:18,420
holds fond memories of my childhood.

412
00:24:18,780 --> 00:24:21,780
Next time,
open Katsutoki Bridge for me, okay?

413
00:24:32,260 --> 00:24:36,700
Let's always smile, okay?

414
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:40,900
Even when something outrageous happens,

415
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:45,400
keep smiling sweetly, okay?

416
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:50,640
Just head out with a
face like nothing's wrong.

417
00:24:50,640 --> 00:24:54,140
Hey, smile for me.

418
00:24:54,140 --> 00:24:57,440
It's not your fault.

419
00:24:57,440 --> 00:25:05,780
Why won't you smile?
Like you were just a moment ago.

420
00:25:05,780 --> 00:25:16,640
Always keep smiling, because a woman
who acts so serious isn't beautiful.

421
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:21,360
You should smile right away.

422
00:25:22,580 --> 00:25:25,840
Unless you're a child, that is.

